<title>HONG KONG: Guoco 1995/96 year net up 15.73 percent.</title>
<headline>Guoco 1995/96 year net up 15.73 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   443.0	 vs 390.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    55.0	  vs 50.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  129.28 gain vs 230.50 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    1,889.05    vs 1,632.35</p>
<p>    Turnover		     11,203.65   vs 8,913.95 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Guoco Group Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  November 13-21</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 22</p>
<p>NOTE - Investment holding company Guoco Group is engaged in banking and financial services, broking and property.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$196.12 million on disposal of investments in subsidiary and associated companies, HK$100.16 million on disposal of investments, HK$93.99 million on disposal of an investment property and loss of HK$260.99 million on compulsory acquisition of land.</p>
<p>Comparative turnover has been adjusted to include the turnover of banking subsidiaries.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 78 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 23 cents) vs 71 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
